3. No paid sale of the Software

Without separate written permission from the relevant copyright holders, you may
not sell the Software to third parties or provide copies, downloads, licenses or
access to the Software for a fee or other consideration. This includes:

- Selling the original Software, modifications or derivatives as paid software;
- Charging for renamed, rebranded, repackaged or recompiled versions;
- Providing software access through paid downloads, subscriptions, activation
  codes, memberships or other consideration;
- Hiding the software price in a bundle, mandatory service fee or other arrangement.

This restriction concerns the paid sale of the Software itself. You may charge
separately for genuine installation, configuration, training, technical support
or custom development services, provided that the Software and the right to use
it remain free of charge and the service fee does not disguise a software sale.
Internal company deployment and use are not sales to third parties.

4. Redistribution and attribution

When distributing the Software or substantial portions covered by this License,
retain this License, existing copyright notices and applicable third-party
licenses and notices, and make them available to recipients. You may not impose
terms that remove recipients' rights under this License to use, modify or
redistribute the Software free of charge.

Distributed modifications must clearly identify their svnbox origin, state that
they have been modified and link to https://github.com/svn-box/svn-box.
Freely distributed modifications may use a different name, but must not
impersonate an official release or imply endorsement by the original authors.
No trademark or branding rights are granted beyond the use necessary to truthfully
identify origin and preserve existing notices.

5. Third-party components and prior grants

Third-party code, runtimes, icons and other components retain their own licenses.
See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md, resources/licenses/ and accompanying upstream
